---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../styles/doge.css';
import '../../../styles/lgr.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Public contracts: what Lancashire's public sector is buying | Tom Pickup"
  description="A searchable record of contracts awarded by Lancashire's councils, police, fire and ambulance services, NHS and other public bodies, drawn from the government's Contracts Finder service, with contract length front and centre: who is paid, how much, for what, and for how long."
>
  <div class="doge-page">
    <nav class="doge-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/lgr/">LGR</a>
      <span class="sep">›</span>
      <span class="here">Public contracts</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="doge-head">
      <span class="doge-eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Public contracts &amp; procurement</span>
      <h1 class="doge-title">What Lancashire's public sector is buying</h1>
      <p class="doge-sub">
        The public sector spends a large part of its money through contracts with outside suppliers. By law those
        contracts are published. Here I bring the Lancashire ones together from the government's own procurement
        service into one searchable record, so you can see who is paid, how much, for what, and crucially for
        how long.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="doge-statband" id="lc-stats">
      <div class="doge-stat"><div class="v teal" id="lc-count">…</div><div class="l">Contracts on record (all public bodies)</div></div>
      <div class="doge-stat"><div class="v" id="lc-value">…</div><div class="l">Value awarded (excluding framework ceilings)</div></div>
      <div class="doge-stat"><div class="v" id="lc-vesting">…</div><div class="l">Council contracts still running on handover day (1 Apr 2028)</div></div>
      <div class="doge-stat"><div class="v" id="lc-longest">…</div><div class="l">Longest term awarded</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="bsp-wrap">
      <div class="bsp-controls">
        <input class="bsp-search" id="lc-search" type="search" placeholder="Search supplier, buyer or what was bought…" aria-label="Search contracts" />
        <select class="bsp-sel" id="lc-group" aria-label="Type of body">
          <option value="">All public bodies</option>
          <option value="council">Councils (reorganised)</option>
          <option value="emergency">Police, fire &amp; ambulance</option>
          <option value="nhs">NHS</option>
          <option value="gov">National agencies</option>
          <option value="education">Colleges &amp; universities</option>
        </select>
        <select class="bsp-sel" id="lc-buyer" aria-label="Buyer"><option value="">Any buyer</option></select>
        <select class="bsp-sel" id="lc-scope" aria-label="Scope">
          <option value="">All contracts</option>
          <option value="vesting">Running past handover (2028)</option>
          <option value="5yr">5 years or longer</option>
          <option value="ext">With an extension option</option>
          <option value="framework">Frameworks only</option>
        </select>
        <select class="bsp-sel" id="lc-sort" aria-label="Sort">
          <option value="value">Highest value first</option>
          <option value="term">Longest term first</option>
          <option value="end">Latest end date first</option>
          <option value="date">Newest first</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <p class="bsp-summary" id="lc-summary">Loading contracts…</p>
      <div class="bsp-tablewrap">
        <table class="bsp-table">
          <thead><tr>
            <th>Buyer &amp; contract</th><th>Supplier</th><th class="num">Value</th><th class="num">Term</th><th class="num">Ends</th>
          </tr></thead>
          <tbody id="lc-tbody"></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="bsp-more"><button class="bsp-morebtn" id="lc-more">Show more</button></div>
    </div>

    <div class="lgr-prose" style="margin-top:1.2rem;">
      <p>
        The data comes from <strong>Contracts Finder</strong>, where public bodies must publish contracts and
        awards above roughly £25,000. It starts with the bodies being reorganised: the <strong>county council
        and thirteen of Lancashire's fourteen borough, city and unitary councils</strong>. Ribble Valley published
        no qualifying contracts, so it does not appear. But councils are not the only public purse in
        Lancashire, and they are not the only landowner: the police, fire and ambulance services, the NHS,
        national agencies and the colleges and universities all hold estate here too. So this page now
        carries their contracts as well.
      </p>
      <p>
        The distinction matters. <strong>Only the councils are abolished by reorganisation</strong>, so only
        their contracts pass to whichever new unitary takes over on <strong>1 April 2028</strong>, whether it
        wants them or not. The police, fire, NHS and the rest are <strong>not</strong> reorganised; they keep
        their own contracts. So the handover figures above count the <strong>council</strong> contracts, while
        the wider bodies are shown as the public-sector landscape around them. Use the filter to move between
        them. As with any of this, the part that matters most for reorganisation is <strong>contract
        length</strong>, so the table leads on term and end date.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doge-disclaimer">
      <strong>Sources and limits.</strong> Contracts are drawn from the Cabinet Office
      <a href="https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/">Contracts Finder</a>, published under the Open
      Government Licence. This is a record of awarded contracts and framework agreements, which are commitments
      to spend, not confirmed payments, and it excludes spending below the publication thresholds. Figures are
      as published by each buyer; where a value was not published, none is shown.
      <strong>On coverage:</strong> the council record is comprehensive on Contracts Finder. The other bodies are
      matched by name, and their coverage is uneven: the <strong>NHS trusts and colleges publish most of their
      tenders elsewhere</strong> (Find a Tender and the NHS Atamis portal), so what is shown here is a floor, not
      their full procurement. National agencies such as National Highways and the Environment Agency have a large
      Lancashire estate but procure nationally, so only contracts with a clear Lancashire link are included, and
      there are few. Only the <strong>councils</strong> are abolished by reorganisation, so the "still running on
      handover day" figure counts council contracts alone.
      <strong>On contract length:</strong> the term shown is the published contract period. Contracts Finder has
      no structured field for extension options, so where a contract says "three years with the option of two
      more", it is flagged <span class="lc-ext">+opt</span>, and where the wording is precise enough the maximum
      is shown as "<span class="lc-ext">up to 5y</span>". Elsewhere the term is a <em>floor</em>: extensions only
      make a contract run longer, so the count still running on handover day is a conservative minimum.
      Frameworks are flagged because actual spend under them commonly outlives the stated term. Inclusion here
      is not a suggestion of any wrongdoing.
    </div>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
  (function () {
    var GRP = { county: 'County council', district: 'District / borough', police: 'Police', fire: 'Fire' };
    function esc(s){ return String(s==null?'':s).replace(/[&<>"]/g,function(c){return {'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;'}[c];}); }
    function money(n){ return n == null ? '' : '£' + Math.round(n).toLocaleString(); }
    var all = [], view = [], shown = 0, PAGE = 60;

    var searchEl = document.getElementById('lc-search');
    var groupEl = document.getElementById('lc-group');
    var buyerEl = document.getElementById('lc-buyer');
    var scopeEl = document.getElementById('lc-scope');
    var sortEl = document.getElementById('lc-sort');
    var tbody = document.getElementById('lc-tbody');
    var summary = document.getElementById('lc-summary');
    var moreBtn = document.getElementById('lc-more');
    var query = '';
    function term(c){
      if (!c.months) return '';
      var y = c.months / 12;
      return y >= 1 ? (Math.round(y * 10) / 10) + ' yr' + (y >= 1.05 ? 's' : '') : c.months + ' mo';
    }
    function pastVesting(c){ return (c.end || '') >= '2028-04-01'; }

    function row(c){
      var tr = document.createElement('tr');
      var td1 = document.createElement('td');
      var sup = document.createElement('div'); sup.className = 'bsp-sup'; sup.textContent = c.title || '(untitled contract)';
      if (c.framework){ var fb = document.createElement('span'); fb.className = 'lc-badge'; fb.textContent = 'framework'; sup.appendChild(document.createTextNode(' ')); sup.appendChild(fb); }
      var meta = document.createElement('div'); meta.className = 'bsp-rowmeta';
      meta.textContent = c.buyer + (c.cat ? ' · ' + c.cat : '');
      td1.appendChild(sup); td1.appendChild(meta);
      if (c.desc) { var d = document.createElement('div'); d.className = 'bsp-rowmeta'; d.textContent = c.desc.slice(0, 150) + (c.desc.length > 150 ? '…' : ''); td1.appendChild(d); }
      var td2 = document.createElement('td'); td2.className = 'bsp-sup'; td2.style.fontWeight = '500';
      td2.textContent = c.supplier || '';
      var td3 = document.createElement('td'); td3.className = 'num bsp-amt'; td3.textContent = money(c.value) || '';
      var td4 = document.createElement('td'); td4.className = 'num bsp-date';
      td4.appendChild(document.createTextNode(term(c) || ''));
      if (c.maxmo && c.maxmo > (c.months || 0)) {
        var mx = document.createElement('span'); mx.className = 'lc-ext';
        mx.textContent = ' up to ' + (Math.round(c.maxmo / 12 * 10) / 10) + 'y';
        mx.title = 'Published term plus a stated extension option';
        td4.appendChild(mx);
      } else if (c.ext) {
        var eo = document.createElement('span'); eo.className = 'lc-ext';
        eo.textContent = ' +opt';
        eo.title = 'Notice mentions an option to extend or renew';
        td4.appendChild(eo);
      }
      var td5 = document.createElement('td'); td5.className = 'num bsp-date';
      td5.textContent = c.end || '';
      if (pastVesting(c)) td5.classList.add('lc-past');
      tr.appendChild(td1); tr.appendChild(td2); tr.appendChild(td3); tr.appendChild(td4); tr.appendChild(td5);
      return tr;
    }
    function apply(){
      view = all.filter(function(c){
        if (groupEl.value && c.gc !== groupEl.value) return false;
        if (buyerEl.value && c.buyer !== buyerEl.value) return false;
        if (scopeEl.value === 'vesting' && !pastVesting(c)) return false;
        if (scopeEl.value === '5yr' && !(c.months >= 60)) return false;
        if (scopeEl.value === 'ext' && !c.ext) return false;
        if (scopeEl.value === 'framework' && !c.framework) return false;
        if (query){
          var hay = ((c.title||'') + ' ' + (c.desc||'') + ' ' + (c.buyer||'') + ' ' + (c.supplier||'')).toLowerCase();
          if (hay.indexOf(query) < 0) return false;
        }
        return true;
      });
      if (sortEl.value === 'term') view.sort(function(a,b){ return (b.months||0) - (a.months||0); });
      else if (sortEl.value === 'end') view.sort(function(a,b){ return (b.end||'').localeCompare(a.end||''); });
      else if (sortEl.value === 'date') view.sort(function(a,b){ return (b.date||'').localeCompare(a.date||''); });
      else view.sort(function(a,b){ return (b.value||0) - (a.value||0); });
      var sum = view.reduce(function(s,c){ return s + (c.value||0); }, 0);
      summary.textContent = '';
      var b1 = document.createElement('b'); b1.textContent = view.length.toLocaleString();
      summary.appendChild(b1); summary.appendChild(document.createTextNode(' contracts'));
      if (sum){ summary.appendChild(document.createTextNode(' worth ')); var b2 = document.createElement('b'); b2.textContent = money(sum); summary.appendChild(b2); }
      summary.appendChild(document.createTextNode(' matching.'));
      tbody.textContent = ''; shown = 0; renderMore();
    }
    function renderMore(){
      var frag = document.createDocumentFragment();
      for (var i = shown; i < view.length && i < shown + PAGE; i++) frag.appendChild(row(view[i]));
      tbody.appendChild(frag); shown = Math.min(shown + PAGE, view.length);
      moreBtn.style.display = shown < view.length ? '' : 'none';
      moreBtn.textContent = 'Show more (' + (view.length - shown).toLocaleString() + ' left)';
    }
    // Rebuild the buyer dropdown to the buyers present in the selected group.
    function populateBuyers(){
      var g = groupEl.value;
      var bs = {};
      all.forEach(function(c){ if (!g || c.gc === g) bs[c.buyer] = true; });
      var cur = buyerEl.value;
      while (buyerEl.options.length > 1) buyerEl.remove(1);
      var keep = false;
      Object.keys(bs).sort().forEach(function(b){
        var o = document.createElement('option'); o.value = b; o.textContent = b; buyerEl.appendChild(o);
        if (b === cur) keep = true;
      });
      buyerEl.value = keep ? cur : '';
    }
    moreBtn.addEventListener('click', renderMore);
    groupEl.addEventListener('change', function(){ populateBuyers(); apply(); });
    [buyerEl, scopeEl, sortEl].forEach(function(s){ s.addEventListener('change', apply); });
    var t; searchEl.addEventListener('input', function(){ clearTimeout(t); t = setTimeout(function(){ query = searchEl.value.toLowerCase().trim(); apply(); }, 180); });

    fetch('/data/lgr-contracts.json').then(function(r){ return r.json(); }).then(function(d){
      all = d.contracts || [];
      var m = d.meta || {};
      var council = m.council || {};
      document.getElementById('lc-count').textContent = (m.total || all.length).toLocaleString();
      document.getElementById('lc-value').textContent = m.sum ? '£' + (m.sum/1e6).toFixed(0) + 'm' : '…';
      // Handover figure is COUNCILS ONLY: only their contracts transfer to the unitaries.
      document.getElementById('lc-vesting').textContent = (council.running_past_vesting_2028 != null) ? council.running_past_vesting_2028.toLocaleString() : '…';
      document.getElementById('lc-longest').textContent = m.max_term_months ? (Math.round(m.max_term_months/12*10)/10) + ' yrs' : '…';
      populateBuyers();
      apply();
    }).catch(function(){ summary.textContent = 'The contracts data could not be loaded.'; });
  })();
  </script>
</Layout>
